# [DD-13b.W1.3] A DEFINITION NAME WITH `-` AND `.` IN IT, and the derived
# prefix. The manager's syntax ruling on the bench's O-13 §4(a): a block name
# admits `-` and `.` after its first byte, and `target = <name>` maps them to
# `_` to produce the C symbol prefix.
#
# ITS POPULATION WOULD OTHERWISE BE ZERO. No corpus file declares a `name`
# at all, so without this fixture the widened grammar, the mapping and the
# `target =` shorthand would all ship with nothing exercising them, and the
# three parsers (pcrec, run.sh, verify_rxt.py) would be compared only on
# names all three already accepted.
target = cls-upto-64
target = ctx.lazy

pattern a+
name cls-upto-64
m "aaa" 0 3

pattern b+
name ctx.lazy
m "bbb" 0 3
